      "category": "bug",
      "title": "Single worker serializes loads; blocked read stalls all hosts",
      "message": "The pump only starts a new job if vellumContentWorkers is 0, so a single worker runs at a time, yet the docs claim up to eight hosts share the job. Worse, when a host is removed while its job is in flight, the worker count is only decremented upon completion, and a blocked read delays all other hosts' loads indefinitely (head-of-line blocking).",
      "suggestion": "Allow a small bounded number of concurrent workers (e.g. 2-4), or time-bound reads so one blocked FIFO or slow filesystem cannot starve all other hosts.",
